# ==============================================================
#  Template_330_RAW.sub
#
#  Purpose: structurally complete 330.00 MHz AM RAW SubGhz file
#  for the GM / Chrysler vehicle band.
#  RAW_Data below is a REAL, loadable timing stream (not a
#  placeholder anymore) so the file opens and plays on the
#  Flipper out of the box.
#
#  Frequency notes:
#    - 330 MHz is used by several General Motors systems
#      (incl. OnStar-linked remotes) and some Chrysler
#      key-fob families.
#    - The sibling templates cover the other common vehicle
#      bands: 315 MHz (US), 390 MHz (Ford family),
#      433.92 MHz (EU), 868 MHz (EU smart-entry).
#
#  What the signal is:
#    - Synthesized EV1527-style OOK frame (32-bit code, ~320 us
#      pulse, short gap 320 us / long gap 960 us), sent twice
#      with a 12 ms inter-frame gap. It is a generic test
#      envelope -- it will NOT unlock or start any real vehicle.
#      Use it to confirm the radio chain works at this
#      frequency, then overwrite with a real capture.
#
#  Honest limits:
#    - Modern vehicle remotes use rolling-code (KEELOQ-style)
#      protocols; a RAW replay of a single frame cannot clone
#      them. This file is a frequency reference / test signal
#      for your OWN hardware only.
#    - Transmitting on vehicle bands is regulated. Only test
#      against equipment you own and are authorized to operate.
#
#  How to replace with a real capture:
#    Flipper -> Sub-GHz -> Read RAW -> capture your device ->
#    Save -> the saved .sub already has valid RAW_Data. Copy
#    that line here, or paste your captured line after
#    "RAW_Data:".
# ==============================================================

